cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ESAC-GI in research, evaluation reports, or comparative claims, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "ESAC-GI: EcoWestern Short and Cheap General Intelligence Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  A short, cheap benchmark that measures difficult capabilities. Forty-two items
  and 75 points across eight categories, 60 of them graded deterministically and
  15 by a pinned open-weight judge. Items are generators rather than stored
  questions, so expected answers are computed rather than remembered, and the
  public repository is the distributable artifact.
type: software
